## Consumed API Endpoints (maps to BACKEND)

> Calls go through the typed client in `lib/api/` (see [BACKEND](./BACKEND.mdc)
> for the authoritative contract). On-chain actions go through `lib/web3/`.

| feature | endpoints / on-chain | phase |
| --- | --- | --- |
| auth | `POST /auth/nonce`, `POST /auth/verify`, `POST /auth/logout`, `GET /auth/me` | `MVP` |
| users | `GET /users/:address`, `PATCH /users/me` | `MVP` |
| projects | `GET /projects`, `GET /projects/:slug`, `POST /projects` 👑, `PATCH /projects/:id` 👑, `POST /projects/:id/transition` 👑 | `MVP` |
| projects | `POST /projects/submit` | `Phase 2` |
| comments | `GET /projects/:id/comments`, `POST /projects/:id/comments`, `DELETE /comments/:id` | `MVP` |
| voting | `GET /projects/:id/votes`, `GET /projects/:id/votes/eligibility`; on-chain `castVote` via `ProjectVoting` | `MVP` |
| scoring | `GET /projects/:id/score`, `GET /projects/:id/score/history` | `MVP` |
| governance | `GET /governance/proposals`, `GET /governance/proposals/:onchainId`; on-chain `propose`/`castVote` via Governor | `MVP` |
| reputation | `GET /reputation/:address` | `MVP → Phase 1` |
| rewards/notifications | `GET /rewards/:address`, `GET /notifications`, `POST /notifications/:id/read` | `Phase 1` |

## Client Data Model & Schemas

> API response types are generated from the backend OpenAPI schema and live in
> `lib/api/`. Form/input validation uses Zod with React Hook Form. Server-cache
> state is held by the data layer; UI/session state lives in Zustand (`store/`).

### Domain types (mirror backend, in `lib/api/types.ts`) `[MVP]`

```ts
export type ProjectState =
  | 'in_analysis' | 'ready' | 'voting' | 'closed' | 'analyzed'

export interface Project {
  id: string
  slug: string
  name: string
  description?: string
  chainId: number
  tokenAddress?: string
  state: ProjectState
  votingContractAddress?: string
  score?: number
  createdAt: string
}

export interface Comment {
  id: string; projectId: string; authorId: string
  body: string; createdAt: string
}

export interface Proposal {
  id: string; onchainId: string; proposerAddress: string; title: string
  description: string | null
  state: 'pending' | 'active' | 'succeeded' | 'defeated' | 'executed'
  startBlock: string | null
  endBlock: string | null
}

export interface Reputation {
  walletAddress: string; eligible: boolean; weight: string
  factors: Record<string, unknown> | null
}
```

### Form schemas (Zod + React Hook Form) `[MVP]`

```ts
// modules/projects/api/schemas.ts
export const createProjectSchema = z.object({
  name: z.string().min(1).max(120),
  description: z.string().optional(),
  chainId: z.number().int(),
  tokenAddress: z.string().optional(),
})

// modules/comments/api/schemas.ts
export const createCommentSchema = z.object({
  body: z.string().min(1).max(5000),
})

// modules/governance/api/schemas.ts  [Phase 1]
export const createProposalSchema = z.object({
  title: z.string().min(1).max(160),
  description: z.string().min(1),
})
```

### Zustand store slices (`store/`) `[MVP]`

```ts
// store/session.ts
interface SessionState {
  user?: { id: string; walletAddress: string; role: 'user'|'team'|'admin' }
  setUser: (u?: SessionState['user']) => void
}

// modules/voting/store.ts
interface VotingState {
  pendingTxHash?: string
  selectedChoice?: number
  setChoice: (c: number) => void
}
```

> Frontend persistence note: the frontend has no SQL store of its own; persistent
> data is modeled in PostgreSQL on the backend (see the SQL Data Modeling section
> of [BACKEND](./BACKEND.mdc)). The client only keeps cached server data + UI state.

## Conventions

- One module = one folder under `modules/`, owning `components/`, `hooks/`,
  `api/`, `store.ts`, `routes.tsx` and `__tests__/`.
- Use Shadcn/UI primitives from `components/ui/`; do not fork them per feature.
- Global/shared state in Zustand (`store/`); feature state in the feature's slice.
- All network calls through the typed client in `lib/api/`; on-chain calls through
  `lib/web3/`.
- Tests: Vitest + Testing Library co-located in `__tests__/`; Playwright e2e in
  `e2e/`. `[MVP]`
